      <main id="content"><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianLogSobolev.gaussian_logSobolev_of_contDiff"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h1>Noncompact C2 Gaussian function log-Sobolev inequality</h1><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianLogSobolev.gaussian_logSobolev_of_contDiff</code> · theorem · <a href="index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h2>Mathematical statement</h2><p class="reader-claim">For every finite-dimensional complete real Hilbert/Borel space E, including rank zero, let gamma be literal stdGaussian E. Every signed real globally C2 f with actual f in L2(gamma), true gradient f in L2(gamma), and Phi(f²) integrable satisfies homogeneous Ent_gamma(f²)&lt;=2 integral norm(gradient f)^2. The actual cutoff mass, entropy and gradient-energy limits are proved internally. Phi(t)=t log t is continuous at zero; neither positive mass nor normalization nor compact support is assumed.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[\operatorname{Ent}_{\gamma}(f^2):=\int\Phi(f^2)\,d\gamma-\Phi\!\left(\int f^2\,d\gamma\right)\le2\int\|\nabla f\|^2\,d\gamma,\quad\gamma=\mathrm{stdGaussian}(E),\quad\Phi(t)=t\log t.\]</div><h3>Proof roadmap</h3><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Derive genuine square and energy domains</strong><p>The two genuine L2 hypotheses imply square and Hilbert-gradient-energy L1. The entropy L1 is the third analytic-domain premise. C2 gives continuity and the true Riesz-gradient measurability needed below; no totalized-integral fallback is used.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Construct actual compact approximants</strong><p>Use the canonical radial cutoff at R_n=n+1, multiply by f, and derive C2compact regularity. One positive derivative constant C is chosen before all radii. Range[0,1] and the real neighborhood plateau come from the same actual cutoff.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Bound the true gradient and identify its limit</strong><p>Apply the real product derivative and Riesz inverse, whose isometry identifies derivative norm with gradient norm. With R_n&gt;=1, the square energy is dominated by2G²+2C²f². For each point the cutoff equals1 on a neighborhood for all sufficiently large radii, so its product has exactly the original true gradient there, including rank0.</p></li><li><span>4</span><strong>Control entropy even where the density vanishes</strong><p>The totalized zero-aware product identity gives Phi(aq)=aPhi(q)+qPhi(a). For0&lt;=a&lt;=1, the lower bound a-1&lt;=Phi(a) and Phi(a)&lt;=0 imply |Phi(a)|&lt;=1. With a=chi_n² and q=f² this gives an integrable dominator without taking log of f or dividing by mass.</p></li><li><span>5</span><strong>Prove all three real integral limits</strong><p>Apply dominated convergence separately with q, |Phi(q)|+q and2G²+2C²q. Every sequence is strongly measurable through actual continuity, every dominator is L1 from the analytic domains, and the pointwise limits are proved using the actual cutoff and gradient plateau.</p></li><li><span>6</span><strong>Pass the compact inequalities without changing the constant</strong><p>Apply actual compact41LSI to each f_n. Continuity of Phi at the limiting mass, including mass0, gives the homogeneous entropy limit. Closed-order convergence passes the inequalities with the unchanged coefficient2.</p></li><li><span>7</span><strong>Exercise the actual noncompact posterior</strong><p>The true standardizedRGO theorem supplies C2, fL2, gradientL2 and qlogqL1 at its actual proximal witness, with f²=q. The Test applies this new result to the raw f=exp(-rho/2)/sqrtZ, without a cutoff certificate or upper step-size restriction. The distinct33KL witness must still be reconciled; GaussianT2/FIRST4.6 remain separate.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h3>All objects and hypotheses</h3><ul><li>E is a finite-dimensional complete real Hilbert space with compatible Borel measurable structure; rank0 is permitted.</li><li>f is signed globally C2; actual MemLp f2 and MemLp true gradient f2 hold under literal gamma.</li><li>Actual Phi(f²) is Integrable gamma. These domain predicates are real32 outputs at the paper consumer, not extra FIRST premises or limit certificates.</li><li>Real Bochner integrals use true L1 domains; coefficient2 is variance1 Gaussian, with homogeneous entropy allowing mass0.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h2>Mathematical proof</h2><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>1. Derive genuine square and energy domains</h4><p>The two genuine L2 hypotheses imply square and Hilbert-gradient-energy L1. The entropy L1 is the third analytic-domain premise. C2 gives continuity and the true Riesz-gradient measurability needed below; no totalized-integral fallback is used.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[f\in L^2(\gamma),\ \nabla f\in L^2(\gamma),\ \Phi(f^2)\in L^1(\gamma)\ \Longrightarrow\ f^2,\|\nabla f\|^2\in L^1(\gamma).\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>MemLp.integrable_sq; memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm; continuous_gradient_of_contDiff_one</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>2. Construct actual compact approximants</h4><p>Use the canonical radial cutoff at R_n=n+1, multiply by f, and derive C2compact regularity. One positive derivative constant C is chosen before all radii. Range[0,1] and the real neighborhood plateau come from the same actual cutoff.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[R_n=n+1,\quad\chi_n=\mathrm{radialSmoothCutoff}(R_n),\quad f_n=\chi_nf,\quad0\le\chi_n\le1,\quad\|D\chi_n\|\le C/R_n.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>radialSmoothCutoff_contDiff; radialSmoothCutoff_hasCompactSupport; radialSmoothCutoff_mem_Icc; radialSmoothCutoff_fderiv_bound</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>3. Bound the true gradient and identify its limit</h4><p>Apply the real product derivative and Riesz inverse, whose isometry identifies derivative norm with gradient norm. With R_n&gt;=1, the square energy is dominated by2G²+2C²f². For each point the cutoff equals1 on a neighborhood for all sufficiently large radii, so its product has exactly the original true gradient there, including rank0.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\nabla f_n=\chi_n\nabla f+f\nabla\chi_n,\quad\|\nabla f_n\|^2\le2\|\nabla f\|^2+2C^2f^2,\quad\nabla f_n(x)=\nabla f(x)\ \text{eventually}.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>gradient_mul; cutoff_energy_bound; cutoff_gradient_eventually_eq; Filter.EventuallyEq.gradient_eq</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>4. Control entropy even where the density vanishes</h4><p>The totalized zero-aware product identity gives Phi(aq)=aPhi(q)+qPhi(a). For0&lt;=a&lt;=1, the lower bound a-1&lt;=Phi(a) and Phi(a)&lt;=0 imply |Phi(a)|&lt;=1. With a=chi_n² and q=f² this gives an integrable dominator without taking log of f or dividing by mass.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\Phi(aq)=a\Phi(q)+q\Phi(a),\quad|\Phi(a)|\le1\ (0\le a\le1),\quad|\Phi(f_n^2)|\le|\Phi(f^2)|+f^2.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>entropy_dilation_bound; Real.negMulLog_mul; Real.self_sub_one_le_mul_log; Real.mul_log_nonpos</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>5. Prove all three real integral limits</h4><p>Apply dominated convergence separately with q, |Phi(q)|+q and2G²+2C²q. Every sequence is strongly measurable through actual continuity, every dominator is L1 from the analytic domains, and the pointwise limits are proved using the actual cutoff and gradient plateau.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\int f_n^2\,d\gamma\to\int f^2\,d\gamma,\quad\int\Phi(f_n^2)\,d\gamma\to\int\Phi(f^2)\,d\gamma,\quad\int\|\nabla f_n\|^2\,d\gamma\to\int\|\nabla f\|^2\,d\gamma.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>cutoff_integral_limits; tendsto_integral_of_dominated_convergence; radialSmoothCutoff_tendsto_one</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>6. Pass the compact inequalities without changing the constant</h4><p>Apply actual compact41LSI to each f_n. Continuity of Phi at the limiting mass, including mass0, gives the homogeneous entropy limit. Closed-order convergence passes the inequalities with the unchanged coefficient2.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\operatorname{Ent}_{\gamma}(f_n^2)\le2\int\|\nabla f_n\|^2\,d\gamma\ \Longrightarrow\ \operatorname{Ent}_{\gamma}(f^2)\le2\int\|\nabla f\|^2\,d\gamma.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>compact_stdGaussian_logSobolev; Real.continuous_mul_log; le_of_tendsto_of_tendsto</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h4>7. Exercise the actual noncompact posterior</h4><p>The true standardizedRGO theorem supplies C2, fL2, gradientL2 and qlogqL1 at its actual proximal witness, with f²=q. The Test applies this new result to the raw f=exp(-rho/2)/sqrtZ, without a cutoff certificate or upper step-size restriction. The distinct33KL witness must still be reconciled; GaussianT2/FIRST4.6 remain separate.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[f(u)=e^{-\rho(u)/2}/\sqrt Z,\quad f^2=q,\quad\operatorname{Ent}_{\gamma}(f^2)\le2\int\|\nabla f\|^2\,d\gamma.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>actual_posterior_noncompact_lsi; standardized_rgo_sqrt_density_domain</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h2>Lean verification</h2><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianLogSobolev.gaussian_logSobolev_of_contDiff"><summary>Lean statement · gaussian_logSobolev_of_contDiff</summary><p>For every finite-dimensional complete real Hilbert/Borel space E, including rank zero, let gamma be literal stdGaussian E. Every signed real globally C2 f with actual f in L2(gamma), true gradient f in L2(gamma), and Phi(f²) integrable satisfies homogeneous Ent_gamma(f²)&lt;=2 integral norm(gradient f)^2. The actual cutoff mass, entropy and gradient-energy limits are proved internally. Phi(t)=t log t is continuous at zero; neither positive mass nor normalization nor compact support is assumed.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem gaussian_logSobolev_of_contDiff
    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
    [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    (f : E → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f)
    (hf2 : MemLp f 2 (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))
    (hgrad2 : MemLp (gradient f) 2 (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))
    (hentropy : Integrable (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2))
      (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)) :
    let γ : Measure E := ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E
    (∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ) -
      (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) * Real.log (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) ≤
      2 * ∫ x, ‖gradient f x‖^2 ∂γ</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gaussianlogsobolev.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianLogSobolev.gaussian_logSobolev_of_contDiff"><summary>Lean proof · gaussian_logSobolev_of_contDiff</summary><p>Derive genuine square and energy domains; Construct actual compact approximants; Bound the true gradient and identify its limit; Control entropy even where the density vanishes; Prove all three real integral limits; Pass the compact inequalities without changing the constant; Exercise the actual noncompact posterior</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem gaussian_logSobolev_of_contDiff
    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
    [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    (f : E → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f)
    (hf2 : MemLp f 2 (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))
    (hgrad2 : MemLp (gradient f) 2 (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))
    (hentropy : Integrable (fun x =&gt; (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2))
      (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)) :
    let γ : Measure E := ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E
    (∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ) -
      (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) * Real.log (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) ≤
      2 * ∫ x, ‖gradient f x‖^2 ∂γ := by
  dsimp only
  let γ := ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E
  let fn := fun n : ℕ =&gt; fun x : E =&gt; radialSmoothCutoff ((n:ℝ)+1) x * f x
  obtain ⟨hm,hp,he⟩ := cutoff_integral_limits γ f hf hf2 hgrad2 hentropy
  have hle (n : ℕ) :
      (∫ x, (fn n x)^2 * Real.log ((fn n x)^2) ∂γ) -
      (∫ x, (fn n x)^2 ∂γ) * Real.log (∫ x, (fn n x)^2 ∂γ) ≤
        2 * ∫ x, ‖gradient (fn n) x‖^2 ∂γ := by
    have hc : ContDiff ℝ 2 (radialSmoothCutoff ((n:ℝ)+1) : E → ℝ) :=
      (radialSmoothCutoff_contDiff (by positivity)).of_le
        (WithTop.coe_le_coe.mpr (le_top : (2 : ℕ∞) ≤ ⊤))
    have hs : HasCompactSupport (fn n) :=
      (radialSmoothCutoff_hasCompactSupport (by positivity)).mul_right
    exact (GaussianCompactHilbertLogSobolev.compact_stdGaussian_logSobolev
      (fn n) (hc.mul hf) hs).2.2.2
  exact le_of_tendsto_of_tendsto
    (hp.sub (Real.continuous_mul_log.continuousAt.tendsto.comp hm))
    (he.const_mul 2) (Eventually.of_forall hle)

end AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianLogSobolev</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gaussianlogsobolev.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details></section><details class="reader-ledger boundary-ledger"><summary>Scope and omitted-condition boundaries</summary><ul><li>Actual stdGaussian E on finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel E, signed globally C2 f with real fL2/gradientL2/Phi(f²)L1 domains. These are produced by actual32 for its true sqrt-density. No cutoff limit/desired inequality/domain-of-repaired-density/law/energy certificate premises. Genuine noncompact function-LSI coefficient2 through internally derived actual cutoff limits; rank0/zero mass retained. Coherent33 KL/Fisher, full weak W12 extension, separate GaussianT2/FIRST4.6/both paper main/error/cost/composition/fullreader remain OPEN. Actual focused3813 passes: true noncompact32 posterior f and its real analytic domains, generic zero and negative constant actualmass4 in every dimension. Independent wholeproof/source/exactcommit/shared admission pending. No coherent33canonicalKL/Fisher or T2/FIRST/main/cost claim.</li></ul></details><details class="proof-reader-provenance reader-ledger"><summary>Sources, dependencies, and reuse</summary><h2>Source and reuse</h2><h3>Samplinglib parents called</h3><ul><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-functionalinequalities-gaussiancompacthilbertlogsobolev-compact-stdgaussian-logsobolev.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianCompactHilbertLogSobolev.compact_stdGaussian_logSobolev</code></a></li><li><a href="../declarations/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-calculus-cutoff-radialsmoothcutoff-cf0c931086.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.Calculus.Cutoff.radialSmoothCutoff</code></a></li><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-calculus-cutoff-radialsmoothcutoff-contdiff.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.Calculus.Cutoff.radialSmoothCutoff_contDiff</code></a></li><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-calculus-cutoff-radialsmoothcutoff-mem-icc.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.Calculus.Cutoff.radialSmoothCutoff_mem_Icc</code></a></li><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-calculus-cutoff-radialsmoothcutoff-eq-one-of-norm-le.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.Calculus.Cutoff.radialSmoothCutoff_eq_one_of_norm_le</code></a></li><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-calculus-cutoff-radialsmoothcutoff-tendsto-one.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.Calculus.Cutoff.radialSmoothCutoff_tendsto_one</code></a></li><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-calculus-cutoff-radialsmoothcutoff-hascompactsupport.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.Calculus.Cutoff.radialSmoothCutoff_hasCompactSupport</code></a></li><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-calculus-cutoff-radialsmoothcutoff-fderiv-bound.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.Calculus.Cutoff.radialSmoothCutoff_fderiv_bound</code></a></li><li><a href="../theorems/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-analysis-calculus-gradient-continuous-gradient-of-contdiff-one.html"><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.Calculus.Gradient.continuous_gradient_of_contDiff_one</code></a></li></ul><h3>Mathlib API called (external library)</h3><ul><li>MemLp.integrable_sq</li><li>memLp_two_iff_integrable_sq_norm</li><li>fderiv_fun_mul</li><li>InnerProductSpace.toDual</li><li>Real.negMulLog_mul</li><li>Real.self_sub_one_le_mul_log</li><li>Real.mul_log_nonpos</li><li>Filter.EventuallyEq.gradient_eq</li><li>Real.continuous_mul_log</li><li>MeasureTheory.tendsto_integral_of_dominated_convergence</li><li>le_of_tendsto_of_tendsto</li></ul><h3>Mathematical sources</h3><ul><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.E6">FIRST S4.E6 / S4.SS1.p4.3 omitted GaussianLSI background; actual32 domain consumer</a> — Actual stdGaussian E on finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel E, signed globally C2 f with real fL2/gradientL2/Phi(f²)L1 domains. These are produced by actual32 for its true sqrt-density. No cutoff limit/desired inequality/domain-of-repaired-density/law/energy certificate premises. Genuine noncompact function-LSI coefficient2 through internally derived actual cutoff limits; rank0/zero mass retained. Coherent33 KL/Fisher, full weak W12 extension, separate GaussianT2/FIRST4.6/both paper main/error/cost/composition/fullreader remain OPEN. Actual focused3813 passes: true noncompact32 posterior f and its real analytic domains, generic zero and negative constant actualmass4 in every dimension. Independent wholeproof/source/exactcommit/shared admission pending. No coherent33canonicalKL/Fisher or T2/FIRST/main/cost claim.</li></ul><p>Samplinglib prose is not a quotation or a source-equivalence certificate. Definitions and aliases are explained as constructions, not counted as new mathematical proofs.</p></details></article></main>
